    "title": "Verizon gets OK to expand Fios",
    "text": "Verizon has been given permission to install underground conduits to support wires and cables at eight sites, including Blueberry Lane and Walnut Street, Arnold Avenue and North Road, North Main Road and America Way, Cedar Lane, North Main Road and Laurel Lane, North Main Road and Rosemary Lane, West Reach Drive and Fly Jib Court, and Westwind Drive.\nThe town council approved the applications at its Dec. 15 meeting. The work will allow Verizon to bring Fios service to these areas.\nThe wireless company is required to secure excavation permits and send notices to homeowners on these roadways. Trenchless installation must be performed at all pavement crossings with no open-trench excavation except for Westwind Drive. The exemption is to protect the sewer force main from damage.",
